<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::service_restriction_inte" target="global_energy_volatility::commodity_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Active technical or policy restrictions on commercial satellite communications degrade remote monitoring, control and automated safety systems for pipelines, LNG facilities and offshore platforms, directly raising the likelihood of operational failures and temporary supply interruptions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::service_restriction_inte" target="global_political_realign::crossborder_signal" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased technical and policy restrictions (throttling, geofencing, access cuts) directly interrupt transnational information and financial flows, reducing the strength and speed of political and informational shock transmission across borders.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_political_realign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::service_restriction_inte" target="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">When commercial satcom services are actively restricted (by providers or states) in the Russia–Ukraine theatre, non-state Iranian-aligned actors that rely on the same global commercial links lose real-time command, targeting and guidance, materially reducing their ability and frequency to mount long-range cross-border strikes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
