<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::information_security_vul" target="global_energy_volatility::energy_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased susceptibility of communications channels to jamming, spoofing or false signals produces spurious outage reports and ambiguous market intelligence, prompting abrupt trading reactions and larger short-term swings in energy prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::information_security_vul" target="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">High-profile jamming, spoofing or interception incidents raise perceived operational and geopolitical risk among investors for firms and markets exposed to the theatre, lowering aggregate risk appetite and sentiment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_political_realign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::information_security_vul" target="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Exposed and exploited information-security weaknesses (spoofing, jamming, comms capture) demonstrated in the Russia–Ukraine war are adopted and adapted by Iranian forces and proxies, improving their ability to degrade adversary sensors and navigation and thereby increasing successful cross‑border strike rates.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::information_security_vul" target="us_china_rivalry::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">High-profile interceptions, spoofing or compromise of communications used in the conflict demonstrate exploitation pathways for AI services and cloud infrastructure, leading investors to downgrade risk appetite for AI startups and projects that rely on exposed commercial comms or insecure supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
