<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" target="global_energy_volatility::commodity_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">More frequent cross-border missile and drone strikes that target or threaten export terminals, pipelines and shipping lanes increase the assessed probability and expected magnitude of near-term physical supply interruptions for energy commodities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" target="global_political_realign::crossborder_signal" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.78</data>
  <data key="d36">Frequent cross-border strikes force neighbouring states and international institutions to issue rapid political/security responses and warnings, accelerating the speed and reach of shock transmission across borders.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_political_realign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" target="russia_ukraine_war::commercial_satcom_access" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher frequency of cross-border strikes increases the probability of direct damage to or operational evacuation of satellite ground infrastructure (earth stations, uplink/downlink facilities) and forces providers to suspend beams over contested airspace, reducing commercial satellite communications availability in theatres relevant to the Russia–Ukraine war.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::cross_border_strike_freq" target="us_china_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in cross‑border strikes tied to actors perceived as backed by regional adversaries accelerates national‑security framing in Washington and allied capitals, triggering faster, broader regulatory and export‑control reviews of AI development and cross‑border tech ties.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
