<edge source="global_political_realign::asset_price_vol" target="global_energy_volatility::energy_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in asset-price volatility trigger margin calls and rapid portfolio rebalancing that force large, abrupt flows into or out of energy futures and physical markets, amplifying realized and implied energy price volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::asset_price_vol" target="russia_ukraine_war::information_security_vul" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in asset-price volatility cause operators and service providers to defer nonessential expenditures and staffing, degrading patching, monitoring and resilience measures and increasing susceptibility of commercial comms to interception, spoofing or jamming.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::asset_price_vol" target="us_china_rivalry::capital_raising_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in asset-price volatility raise the effective cost of capital and close IPO/secondary windows, causing venture and public capital-raising for AI firms to pause or shrink until markets stabilize.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="global_political_realign::investor_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="global_political_realign::asset_price_vol" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="global_political_realign::crossborder_signal" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="iran_regional_escalation::energy_supply_risk_premi" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Deteriorating investor risk sentiment tied to geopolitical realignment causes traders and funds to widen risk premia on energy contracts, directly raising the market component priced as disruption risk for supply chains in the region.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="russia_ukraine_war::commercial_satcom_access" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved investor risk sentiment lowers financing costs and unlocks capital for satellite launches, ground infrastructure and capacity leases, increasing available commercial satcom bandwidth and coverage serving the theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_political_realign::investor_sentiment" target="us_china_rivalry::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">An improvement (or deterioration) in investor risk sentiment directly changes portfolio allocations for AI sectors—better sentiment causes allocators to accept higher valuation and operational risk in AI investments while worse sentiment causes immediate de-risking.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_political_realign</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
